{"id": "EUVD-2026-102259", "enisaUuid": "110d4bc8-328a-34ab-b9b2-33c932eb5784", "description": "GNOME libgxps through 0.3.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds read in path_geometry_start_element() that allows attackers to read past allocations via crafted PolyBezierSegment or PolyQuadraticBezierSegment Points attributes. Attackers can supply a point count not divisible by three or two in a crafted XPS document to crash consumers like Evince and render adjacent heap memory into output.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:52", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libgxps-poly-segment-points-arity-oob-read", "https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgxps/-/blob/f5027ed09c767e8a02e652fbc77dcea79e19e10d/libgxps/gxps-path.c#L776-L785", "https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgxps/-/blob/f5027ed09c767e8a02e652fbc77dcea79e19e10d/libgxps/gxps-path.c#L832-L848", "https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgxps", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gnome-libgxps-through-0.3.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-path-geometry-start-element"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111132", "GHSA-28f7-fxcp-c8vq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1cf3cd6c-67bc-3d1c-a7b6-908239aae94f", "product": {"name": "libgxps", "vendor": {"name": "Gnome"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ef7b08c8-b0c9-395c-ba8f-16a86dfc316b", "vendor": {"name": "Gnome"}}], "isExploited": false}